{"type":"text","timestamp":1788197576795,"sessionID":"ses_fa7209727ffeT66IcUCHQCxw4C","part":{"id":"prt_058e18a58001liZvmWen7FWz5f","messageID":"msg_058e1831400177z2zeCx92kBK6","sessionID":"ses_fa7209727ffeT66IcUCHQCxw4C","type":"text","text":"Done. The book collection REST API is implemented and working.\n\n## Summary\n\nBuilt with **Python stdlib only** (no framework installed in venv — used `http.server` + `sqlite3`), so zero pip installs needed.\n\n**Files written:**\n- `bookdb.py` — thread-safe SQLite persistence layer (`BookDB`) with CRUD over a `books` table.\n- `app.py` — HTTP server + a pure `BookAPI.dispatch(method, path, query, body)` function for testability; `BookHTTPRequestHandler` adapts it to HTTP. Implements all endpoints, JSON responses, correct status codes (201/200/204/400/404/500), and `?author=` filtering.\n- `README.md` — setup, run, endpoint table, curl examples.\n- `test_dispatch.py` — 14 unit tests (health, CRUD, validation of required/non-empty title & author, year type check, 404s, filtering).\n- `test_http.py` — 4 integration tests over a live socket (health, full CRUD flow, 400 on bad input, 404 on missing).\n\n**Results:**\n- `pytest -q` → **18 passed**.\n- Live smoke test confirms `/health`, create, list, 400, and 404 all return correct responses.\n\nRun with `python app.py` (defaults to `127.0.0.1:8000`, persists to `books.db`).","time":{"start":1788197571160,"end":1788197576791}}}
